<title>MEXICO: VW's Mexico unit hikes wages 20 pct, avoids strike.</title>
<headline>VW's Mexico unit hikes wages 20 pct, avoids strike.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Mexican unit of Volkswagen AG has awarded 11,000 workers at its Puebla plant a 20 percent salary increase and avoided a strike scheduled for Monday, national radio said.</p>
<p>Radio Red, citing the Labor Ministry, said the unions and management agreed to the wage hike over the weekend. It did not say when the salary increase would be implemented. No other details were given.</p>
<p>VW spokesmen at the Puebla plant, 60 miles (100km) east of Mexico City were not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom +525 7289530))</p>
